meta {
  name: OAuth Google Callback
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Google OAuth 2.0 callback handler. Called after user grants consent.
  Flow:
    1. Receives authorization code from Google via Supabase redirect.
    2. Exchanges code for a Supabase session via `exchangeCodeForSession()` (PKCE).
    3. Enforces email verification gate (PRD §5.1): if email_confirmed_at is null, session is deleted and 401 is returned.
    4. New users get a tenant auto-provisioned via the Supabase database trigger `handle_verified_user`.
    5. Redirects to {FRONTEND_URL}/oauth-callback with access_token and refresh_token as query params.
  Returns: HTTP 302 to frontend on success, or 302 with error param if failed.
  Internal classification: PUBLIC (no auth token required).
}
